※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=-4 diag=none

※ Dividing by zero has no answer, and the three architectures do three
※ different things about it: one raises a fault of the processor's own, one
※ answers with all ones, one with zero.  So it is asked about first, and the
※ program stops the same way on all three.

let hundred: u8 = 100u8
let none: u8 = 0u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    hundred ÷ none
